SN  - 1877-0509
DO  - https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procs.2026.06.068
UR  - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1877050926016996
KW  - Prompt Injection
KW  - Explainable AI (XAI)
KW  - SHAP Explanations
KW  - Leave-One-Out (LODO) Analysis
KW  - Malicious Prompt Detection
AB  - Large language Models are becoming part of a greater number of digital products, ranging from critical banking and finance infrastructure to educational platforms. These advancements in Artificial Intelligence have been mirrored by an increase in several security vulnerabilities and one of the most critical vulnerability is Prompt Injection. In prompt injection, an attacker manipulates input in order to bypass safety controls. The current detection mechanisms like embedding-based classifiers achieve high accuracy but relying entirely on a binary ”block-or-allow ” strategy disintegrates user experience, underscoring the need for sanitization techniques that offset threats while keep original user intent intact. This research found that conventional Explainable AI(XAI) tools like SHapley Additive exPlanations(SHAP) sometimes fail to identify the words that are responsible for the malicious behavior, especially in complex compound phrases. In order to address this shortcoming, we have established a novel Leave-One-Out(LODO) framework. This framework measures the influence of a token towards malicious behavior by iteratively discarding them and then re-assessing the prompts maliciousness. Through our approach, we validated on the Malicious Prompt Detection Dataset (MPDD) using an XGBoost Classifier with sentence-embeddings and achieved accuracy of approximately 95% along with a probabilistic Markov Chain model that captured prompt structures with 90.79% accuracy. This approach combines LODO diagnostics with semantic token replacement. The outcomes support that this impact-based reasoning lays out more unerring basis for identifying and replacing malicious components compared to attribution-based methods, licensing practical, intent-preserving prompt sanitization.
ER  - 
